# Project local
*.log
*.tmp

# vibe-ic#361, producer side. The `*.log` rule above is right for build noise
# and wrong for EVIDENCE: a sign-off report that cites `foo.log` as its proof
# could never ship that proof, because the ignore rule silently dropped it.
# The gate added for #361 blocks a NEW dangling citation; this is the other
# half — logs that live beside the reports they prove are deliverables. Adds
# in this repo are always explicit paths, so nothing is swept in by this.
!benchmark-data/**/reports/**/*.log
# vibe-ic review F10, the other half of the same hole. The rescue above covers
# `reports/**` only, and a formal proof transcript does not live there: the
# runner writes it beside its task, at `phase2/stage1/formal/<stem>.sby.log`.
# So `formal_evidence.json` — which DOES ship, being under `reports/` — could
# cite `phase2/stage1/formal/formal_<top>_formal.sby.log` while the ignore rule
# silently dropped the very file it points at. MEASURED on 135ce027a: all three
# published spm PDK cells cite exactly that path, all three genuinely ran the
# proof (each cell's own phase2_one_shot.json lists `formal/results.json` in
# phase2_manifests.output_files, a path the runner appends ONLY on the
# proved-and-all_proved branch), and ZERO of the transcripts are tracked. Not
# an authoring slip in one campaign — the structurally guaranteed outcome for
# every design, because the citation and its proof sat on opposite sides of
# this rule. Deliberately narrow: `*.sby.log` is the runner's own transcript
# filename, so SymbiYosys task-workdir noise (model/design.log, design_prep.log)
# stays ignored and nothing is swept in by a wide add.
!benchmark-data/**/formal/**/*.sby.log
# The SAME hole, one runner-generation earlier, found by a test of mine that
# went red in CI and green here. F10's rescue above matches `*.sby.log`, which
# is how the CURRENT runner names its transcript. An older one writes
# `sby_<top>.log`, and `benchmark-data/ic/subservient` ships a published,
# PASS-verdict `formal_evidence.json` citing exactly that — at a path the repo
# did not contain. A narrow rule and a naming change are all it takes for the
# citation and its proof to end up on opposite sides again, which is why this
# negation is by PREFIX rather than by suffix. MEASURED before widening: this
# pattern matches three files repo-wide, two already tracked
# (`reset_safety/sby_reset_safety*.log`, force-added by #411 as the
# deliverables they are) and the one above. The obvious wider rule,
# `formal/**/*.log`, would sweep in SymbiYosys workdir noise —
# `model/design.log`, `design_prep.log`, `design_aiger.log` — so it is not
# used. Adds here are always explicit paths; nothing is swept in by this.
!benchmark-data/**/formal/**/sby_*.log
.env
.env.local

# Private commercial-PDK config (NDA). Resolved at runtime by
# plugins/vibe-ic/programs/_commercial_pdk.py from $VIBEIC_PRIVATE_CONFIG or
# ~/.config/vibeic/commercial_pdk.json (both OUTSIDE the repo by default). This
# defensively ignores any repo-local copy so the private SKU never gets tracked.
**/commercial_pdk.json
.config/vibeic/

