*.rda
work/
runs/
# vibe-ic#1744 — the SAME evidence-vs-noise line the `*.log` block above draws,
# for a directory name. `runs/` is right for EDA flow output in a project tree
# and wrong for the ONE run directory that is a tracked test fixture: the
# external shuttle precheck writes `runs/<tag>/<NN>-<step>/`, and the parser in
# `tapeout_readiness_check` keys on that structure — specifically on which step
# dirs carry a `state_out.json`. A fixture that renamed `runs/` to dodge this
# rule would stop being what the tool emits, which is the only property that
# makes it worth having. MEASURED: without these two lines `git add -A` stages
# PROVENANCE.md and silently drops all fourteen evidence files, so the test
# would import a fixture that is not there.
!vibe-ic-marketplace/plugins/vibe-ic/programs/tests/fixtures/shuttle_precheck_refusal/runs/
!vibe-ic-marketplace/plugins/vibe-ic/programs/tests/fixtures/shuttle_precheck_refusal/runs/**

